# Repo-wide safety net.
#
# Every engine carries its own .gitignore, which is the right place for
# engine-specific artifacts (seeded databases, fetched benchmark logs, server
# logs). This file exists so the universal ones cannot slip through when a new
# engine is added before its own ignore file is written — which is exactly how
# four engines ended up with build output committed.

node_modules/
dist/
build/

# TypeScript incremental build state. Machine-local, and it changes on every
# compile, so a tracked copy produces a diff on every branch it touches.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local configuration never belong in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

coverage/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
